---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Victor Saly Arcade"
  description="What Victor Saly Arcade stores when you sign in, what it does not, and how to delete it. No email address is collected and nothing is shared with anyone."
  path="/privacy"
>

  <header class="intro">
    <p class="kicker"><a href="/">Victor Saly Arcade</a></p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">Victor Saly Arcade is the collection of free browser games at
      <a href="https://shutthecube.com">shutthecube.com</a> and
      <a href="https://delulubeats.com">delulubeats.com</a>, and the shared leaderboard behind them.
      This policy covers all of it.</p>
    <p class="updated">Last updated 2 September 2026</p>
  </header>

  <main id="main" class="policy">

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>You can play every game completely without an account, and nothing you do leaves your device.
      Signing in is optional and does exactly one thing: it puts a name next to your score on the
      daily leaderboard. If you sign in we store an anonymous Google account identifier and a display
      name. <strong>We never ask for or receive your email address.</strong> You can delete everything
      from inside the game at any time, and it is gone immediately.</p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>These games are made and run by Victor Saly, an individual developer based in London, United
      Kingdom, who is the data controller for the purposes of UK and EU data protection law. You can
      reach me at <a href="mailto:info@victorsaly.com">info@victorsaly.com</a> about anything on this
      page, including a request to see or delete your data.</p>

    <h2>Playing without signing in</h2>
    <p>The games keep your progress, high scores, averages, win rates, streaks and display
      preferences in your own browser's local storage. This stays on your device, is used only to
      make the games work between visits, and is never transmitted anywhere. No account is required
      to play anything.</p>
    <p>You can clear it at any time through your browser's site-data or local-storage settings.</p>

    <h2>If you sign in to the leaderboard</h2>
    <p>Signing in uses Google. We request only the <code>openid</code> and <code>profile</code>
      scopes, which give us an opaque account identifier and a basic profile name. We do not request
      the <code>email</code> scope, so we never receive your email address, and we request nothing
      that would let us read anything else in your Google account.</p>

    <p>What is stored on our server:</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>An opaque Google account identifier</td><td>To recognise you as the same player next time you sign in.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>A display name</td><td>Shown next to your score. It starts as your Google first name and you can change it to anything.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Your scores</td><td>The score, whether you finished the board, how many turns it took, which daily board it was, and a record of the moves you played.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>The record of moves exists so that a submitted score can be checked against the board it
      claims to come from. It is what keeps invented scores off the leaderboard, and it contains
      nothing about you &mdash; only which tiles were played.</p>

    <p>We do <strong>not</strong> store your email address, your Google profile picture, or any
      Google access or refresh token. We do not use advertising, we do not sell or share data with
      anyone, and there are no third-party tracking cookies.</p>

    <h2>What is public</h2>
    <p>Your display name and your scores appear on the leaderboard, which anyone can open. Nothing
      else about you is shown. Please do not choose a display name you would rather strangers did not
      see &mdash; you can change it at any time from the leaderboard.</p>

    <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
    <p>Open the leaderboard inside any game and choose <strong>Delete my data</strong>. This
      immediately and permanently removes your account record and every score you have posted. There
      is no waiting period, no soft delete, and no copy kept.</p>
    <p>Signing out instead simply ends the session and leaves your scores in place.</p>

    <h2>Legal basis, retention and transfers</h2>
    <p>Where UK or EU data protection law applies, the basis for storing your display name and scores
      is your consent, given by choosing to sign in and withdrawn by deleting your data. Scores are
      kept until you delete them, because a leaderboard that forgets is not a leaderboard. You have
      the right to access, correct, export or erase your data, and to complain to the UK Information
      Commissioner's Office.</p>
    <p>The leaderboard runs on Cloudflare Workers and Cloudflare D1, and data may be processed on
      Cloudflare's global network, including outside the UK and EEA, under Cloudflare's own data
      protection terms.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The games are suitable for all ages and can be played in full without an account. Signing in
      requires a Google account, and Google applies its own minimum age requirements. We do not
      knowingly collect data from children below the age of digital consent in their country; if you
      believe a child has signed in, email me and I will delete the record.</p>

    <h2>Other services involved</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong> hosts the game sites.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts this site and runs the leaderboard.</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> handles sign-in, under its own privacy policy.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Each may process limited technical information such as IP address and request logs in order to
      deliver the service. The games themselves load no third-party scripts at runtime &mdash; signing in
      works by sending your browser to Google and back, not by embedding Google's code in the page.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If these games begin using analytics, advertising, or anything else that processes personal
      information, this page will be updated before that change takes effect.</p>

  </main>

</Base>

<style>
  .updated { color: var(--muted); font-size: .88rem; margin: .8rem 0 0; }
  .policy h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 2rem 0 .5rem; }
  .policy h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .policy p, .policy li { max-width: 62ch; color: var(--ink-2); line-height: 1.65; }
  .policy ul { padding-left: 1.1rem; }
  .policy li { margin: .35rem 0; }
  .policy table { border-collapse: collapse; margin: .8rem 0; font-size: .93rem; }
  .policy th, .policy td { text-align: left; padding: .5rem .8rem .5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft); vertical-align: top; }
  .policy th { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
</style>
